Fix: raw JSON tool calls dropped when a stray closing ``` trails them.

StreamingToolDetector.processNormalState() always preferred a code-fence
match over a raw-JSON match, even when the fence match occurred LATER in
the buffered text. When Lumo emits a raw (unfenced) tool call and appends
a stray, unmatched closing ``` out of habit -- and both land in the same
chunk -- the detector mistakes that trailing ``` for an opening fence and
swallows the entire preceding JSON as inert text. The tool call is never
attempted, so opencode gets a text response instead of a function call
and the agent turn just stops.

Fix: only take the fence branch when the fence match occurs at or before
any raw-JSON start in the current buffer.

--- a/src/api/tools/streaming-tool-detector.ts
+++ b/src/api/tools/streaming-tool-detector.ts
@@ -90,9 +90,19 @@
